WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.995
This video shows which calendar feature to turn on for each job, how

00:00:04.995 --> 00:00:09.369
to copy calendars, their events and their categories to another site with a

00:00:09.369 --> 00:00:13.256
deployment plan, what the import does and does not do, and what to

00:00:13.256 --> 00:00:15.470
check when something does not work.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.559
Open Tools, then Features, and search for Calendars.

00:00:23.559 --> 00:00:27.720
Each feature adds one thing, so you turn on only what you need.

00:00:30.177 --> 00:00:32.092
Calendars is the base:

00:00:32.092 --> 00:00:39.545
the calendar view, shared and personal calendars, events, sharing, and the recipe and deployment steps.

00:00:39.545 --> 00:00:44.332
Team, Resource and Office Calendars each add kinds of calendars:

00:00:44.332 --> 00:00:47.477
teams, rooms and equipment, and offices.

00:00:47.929 --> 00:00:51.524
Calendar Reminders adds the on-screen reminders.

00:00:51.524 --> 00:00:55.718
Calendar Invitations emails invitations, and needs email.

00:00:55.718 --> 00:01:00.511
Calendar Feeds adds subscription addresses, and export and import.

00:01:00.511 --> 00:01:04.439
External Calendars shows another calendar, read only.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:09.949
Calendars API adds web endpoints for other systems, and has no screen of its own.

00:01:09.949 --> 00:01:11.169
It is off here.

00:01:11.169 --> 00:01:15.007
Each feature lists what it depends on, so you can see what a

00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:17.390
feature needs before you enable it.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:23.193
To share company and personal calendars, turn on Calendars.

00:01:23.193 --> 00:01:28.172
For teams, add Team Calendars, which also adds the page that shows when

00:01:28.172 --> 00:01:29.530
a team is free.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:34.521
To book meeting rooms and equipment, add Resource Calendars.

00:01:34.521 --> 00:01:39.210
To track who is in an office, and book desks, add Office Calendars.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:48.976
For invitations, reminders, subscriptions and external calendars, add Calendar Invitations, Calendar Reminders, Calendar

00:01:48.976 --> 00:01:51.480
Feeds, or External Calendars.

00:01:55.671 --> 00:02:00.403
Open Tools, Deployments, Plans, and choose Add Deployment Plan.

00:02:00.403 --> 00:02:02.391
Name it Copy calendars.

00:02:05.305 --> 00:02:08.975
Choose Add Step, and find Calendars in the list.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:14.316
Include events takes every calendar's events.

00:02:14.316 --> 00:02:20.854
Include categories, ticked by default, takes everyone's categories, so the events keep their colors.

00:02:20.854 --> 00:02:23.630
Tick Include events, and choose Create.

00:02:24.081 --> 00:02:25.320
Choose Execute.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:28.094
File Download exports the plan as a file.

00:02:28.094 --> 00:02:32.875
Import it on the other site with Package Import, under Deployments, or send

00:02:32.875 --> 00:02:34.881
it with a remote deployment.

00:02:39.081 --> 00:02:43.946
The import creates what is missing and updates what is already there, matched

00:02:43.946 --> 00:02:45.939
by each record's identifier.

00:02:45.939 --> 00:02:49.691
Importing the same file twice does not duplicate anything.

00:02:50.441 --> 00:02:54.733
A calendar needs the feature of its kind to be on at the other site.

00:02:54.733 --> 00:02:57.691
A room needs Resource Calendars, for example.

00:02:58.441 --> 00:03:03.631
Imported events are not checked for overlaps, and they send no invitations.

00:03:03.631 --> 00:03:07.476
A recipe with the Calendars step behaves the same way.

00:03:07.476 --> 00:03:11.641
For the exact shape, export first and start from that file.

00:03:15.841 --> 00:03:17.859
You cannot see a calendar:

00:03:17.859 --> 00:03:20.635
it is private and not shared with you.

00:03:20.635 --> 00:03:24.671
Ask its owner to share it, or to make it shared or public.

00:03:25.421 --> 00:03:28.226
You can see the time but not the event:

00:03:28.226 --> 00:03:32.401
you can only see free and busy time, or the event is private.

00:03:33.151 --> 00:03:37.339
An event is refused as already booked, or as already full:

00:03:37.339 --> 00:03:42.510
a room, a piece of equipment or the office has no room left at that time.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.211
Choose another time.

00:03:44.961 --> 00:03:47.031
No invitation email arrives:

00:03:47.031 --> 00:03:51.903
check that email works, that Calendar Invitations is on, and that the site

00:03:51.903 --> 00:03:53.182
has a Base url.

00:03:53.182 --> 00:03:55.861
Without it, there are no answer links.

00:03:57.861 --> 00:04:03.035
Turn on the features you need, and move calendars between sites with a deployment plan.

00:04:03.035 --> 00:04:04.481
Thanks for watching.

